course: dictionary
lesson: 10130
title: Threadworm: a tiny worm in the gut
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A threadworm is a tiny white worm, as thin as a piece of thread. It can live for a while in the gut, which is the long tube inside your body that digests your food. Read this sentence: «Threadworms are tiny white worms in the gut that come out at night to lay eggs, causing an itchy bottom.» The clue words tiny, white and gut tell you what they look like and where they live.
explain: The sentence also gives you a clue about the itch. «Causing an itchy bottom» tells you the worms cause the itch, so the itch is the sign that something is wrong. A word like parasite may be new to you, but the sentence helps: a parasite lives on another living thing, and a threadworm lives inside a person.
fact: A threadworm is a tiny white worm, like a piece of thread.
fact: Threadworms are very common in children, and having them does not mean you are dirty.
fact: Tiny eggs can get on your fingers, then into your mouth, so they spread.
fact: Washing your hands, scrubbing under your nails, not biting your nails and washing bedding all help to stop them.
fact: A threadworm is a parasite, which means it lives on or in another living thing.
exercise: «Threadworms are tiny white worms in the gut.» What is a threadworm? | A sort of bread | *A tiny white worm, like a piece of thread | A big brown beetle | A type of medicine from the chemist
exercise: «Threadworms cause an itchy bottom, especially at night.» Where is the itch? | Inside the ears | *Around the bottom | On the knees | In the hair
exercise: Why does washing your hands help stop threadworms? | *It stops the tiny eggs getting from your fingers into your mouth | It cures the itch straight away | It makes the worms shrink | It stops you feeling tired
test: What does parasite mean? | *Something that lives on or in another living thing | A tiny white worm | A large animal that lives in the sea | A sort of medicine
test: Does having threadworms mean you are dirty? | Yes, but only at night | Yes, always | *No, they are very common in children | Only if you wash too often
exam: Jayden reads «The whole family is treated» and asks what treated means. What does it most likely mean here? | Taken to a doctor's waiting room for a long time | Brought some sweets for the family | Asked to clean the bedding | *Given medicine to get rid of the worms
